{"bundle_id":"9a1265b4d8b9b713b81b82f999242c72","candidates":[{"id":"redis2/orphan-cleanup-replica-read-recheck","verdict":"confirmed","basis":"Trigger holds. redis_cluster2 with useReadOnly or routeByLatency sets ClusterOptions.ReadOnly, and go-redis then sends read-only commands (GET, EXISTS) to a replica of the key's slot. The value key is keyPrefix+path and the index key is keyPrefix+dir+"\x00", with no hash tag, so they sit in different slots with independent replication. ListDirectoryEntries reads the members from a replica of the index shard, then FindEntry does a GET on a replica of the value shard. A lagging value replica returns redis.Nil, which becomes ErrNotFound and calls removeOrphanedDirectoryListMember. That function does ZREM on the index master, then EXISTS, which is also routed to a replica (probably the same lagging one). EXISTS returns 0, the function returns at line 247, and the live entry's member stays removed. At the merge-base a not-found result only hit `continue`, so the lag cost one listing. At head the loss is permanent, because UpdateEntry (lines 92-95) only calls doInsertEntry and never re-adds the member. The PR body says "Only a positively confirmed absent value leaves the member removed" and "behaves identically on all three transports". The re-check is not a positive confirmation when it reads the same replica class as the failed GET. I did not run the test: no Redis is available offline, and the changed tests skip without RUN_REDIS_TESTS.","evidence":[{"coordinate":"weed/filer/redis2/universal_redis_store.go:245-248","text":"exists, err := store.Client.Exists(ctx, store.getKey(string(path))).Result()
	if err == nil && exists == 0 {
		return
	}"},{"coordinate":"weed/filer/redis2/universal_redis_store.go:99-101","text":"data, err := store.Client.Get(ctx, store.getKey(string(fullpath))).Result()
	if err == redis.Nil {
		return nil, filer_pb.ErrNotFound"},{"coordinate":"weed/filer/redis2/universal_redis_store.go:39-44,254","text":"getKey returns store.keyPrefix + key; genDirectoryListKey returns dir + DIR_LIST_MARKER ("\x00"), so the value key path and the index key dir+"\x00" carry no hash tag"},{"coordinate":"weed/filer/redis2/universal_redis_store.go:92-95","text":"func (store *UniversalRedis2Store) UpdateEntry(ctx context.Context, entry *filer.Entry) (err error) {

	return store.doInsertEntry(ctx, entry)"},{"coordinate":"weed/filer/redis2/redis_cluster_store.go:48-58","text":"ReadOnly: readOnly, RouteByLatency: routeByLatency ... store.Client = redis.NewClusterClient(options)"},{"coordinate":"go-redis v9.21.0 osscluster.go:2399-2402 (clone-cache/gomodcache/github.com/redis/go-redis/v9@v9.21.0)","text":"if c.opt.ReadOnly {
		cmdInfo := c.cmdInfo(ctx, cmdName)
		if cmdInfo != nil && cmdInfo.ReadOnly {
			return c.slotReadOnlyNode(state, slot)"},{"coordinate":"weed/filer/redis_conf/redis_conf.go:63-76","text":"ApplyToCluster sets only retry, timeout and pool options; it does not change ReadOnly or routing"}],"corrections":{"change":"Restore the rule "a value-key GET or EXISTS result may drop an index member only if it came from the primary of the value key's slot" for every path that drops a member. In removeOrphanedDirectoryListMember, do the confirming absence check on the master of the value key's slot (an EVAL/EVALSHA-based EXISTS, or another command go-redis does not mark read-only). Alternatively skip the ZREM cleanup entirely when the store was built with ReadOnly or RouteByLatency, which needs the redis_cluster2 store to record that flag. Keep the ZREM then re-check then ZAddNX compensating order for the concurrent-insert race. Moving the check before the ZREM would not close that race."},"safety_rulings":[{"path":"ListDirectoryEntries -> FindEntry -> removeOrphanedDirectoryListMember on a cluster client with ReadOnly or RouteByLatency","conditions":"value-shard replica lags the SET while the index-shard replica has applied the ZADD","premise":"The EXISTS re-check reliably confirms the value is absent","ruling":"fails","evidence":[{"coordinate":"go-redis v9.21.0 osscluster.go:2438-2451","text":"slotReadOnlyNode returns slotClosestNode/slotRandomNode/slotSlaveNode, never the master, for read-only commands"},{"coordinate":"weed/filer/redis2/universal_redis_store.go:245-247","text":"exists, err := store.Client.Exists(...); if err == nil && exists == 0 { return }"}]},{"path":"Same path on a primary-routed client (single server, failover client, or cluster without ReadOnly/RouteByLatency)","conditions":"GET and EXISTS both reach the master, so they see writes in order","premise":"Steady-state invariant: a value key existing must never be observed with its index member missing after the cleanup finishes. Under primary routing this holds, so the defect is confined to replica-read configs.","ruling":"holds","evidence":[{"coordinate":"weed/filer/redis2/universal_redis_store.go:86","text":"store.Client.Set(ctx, store.getKey(string(entry.FullPath)), value, ...) runs before the ZAddNX at line 68"},{"coordinate":"weed/filer/redis2/universal_redis_store.go:250","text":"store.Client.ZAddNX(ctx, dirListKey, redis.Z{Score: 0, Member: fileName})"},{"coordinate":"weed/filer/redis_conf/redis_conf.go:63-76","text":"ApplyToCluster does not set ReadOnly, RouteByLatency or RouteRandomly"}]},{"path":"Sibling interleavings on a primary-routed client: cleanup ZREM/EXISTS versus a concurrent InsertEntry SET/ZAddNX","conditions":"GET returned nil, so it precedes the SET. Either ZREM is before the ZAddNX (which then adds the member) or after it (then the EXISTS follows the SET and restores).","premise":"The rule holds for the insert-versus-cleanup pair on the primary. The replica-read failure is a separate sibling that the change must close.","ruling":"holds","evidence":[{"coordinate":"weed/filer/redis2/universal_redis_store.go:86","text":"SET value happens before"},{"coordinate":"weed/filer/redis2/universal_redis_store.go:245-250","text":"EXISTS is issued after ZREM, and ZAddNX restores when it sees the value"}]}]}],"premises":[{"id":"premise-1","ruling":"holds","evidence":[{"coordinate":"weed/filer/redis2/universal_redis_store.go:86","text":"store.Client.Set(ctx, store.getKey(string(entry.FullPath)), value, ...) is the first write of InsertEntry, via doInsertEntry at line 58"},{"coordinate":"weed/filer/redis2/universal_redis_store.go:99-101","text":"FindEntry returns ErrNotFound only when the GET returned redis.Nil, so on a primary the GET precedes the insert's SET"},{"coordinate":"weed/filer/redis2/universal_redis_store.go:245-250","text":"the EXISTS follows the ZREM, so if the SET has happened by then the member is re-added; if it has not, the insert's later ZAddNX runs after the ZREM and adds it"},{"coordinate":"weed/filer/redis/../redis_conf/redis_conf.go:63-76","text":"cluster settings never enable ReadOnly, RouteByLatency or RouteRandomly, and the sentinel store uses redis.NewFailoverClient (redis_sentinel_store.go:56), which routes to the master"}]},{"id":"premise-2","ruling":"fails","failed_step":"Line 238: ZREM returns a non-nil error although the server already executed it. Examples are a ctx cancellation or read timeout after the command was sent, or exhausted retries. Line 239 then returns without the EXISTS re-check or ZAddNX restore. If a concurrent InsertEntry's ZAddNX was a no-op because the member was still present, the live entry loses its member. This needs a concurrent recreate coinciding with an ambiguous Redis error, the same coincidence the premise already accepts for the final ZAddNX.","evidence":[{"coordinate":"weed/filer/redis2/universal_redis_store.go:238-240","text":"if err := store.Client.ZRem(ctx, dirListKey, fileName).Err(); err != nil {
		return
	}"},{"coordinate":"weed/filer/redis2/universal_redis_store.go:68","text":"store.Client.ZAddNX(...) in InsertEntry is a no-op when the member is still present, so an insert that races ahead of the ZREM leaves nothing to restore the member if the ZREM error path returns early"},{"coordinate":"weed/filer/redis2/universal_redis_store.go:245-250","text":"EXISTS errors and a zero result are handled: an EXISTS error falls through to the ZAddNX restore, so only the ZREM error branch and the final ZAddNX are unguarded"}]}],"duplicate_groups":[],"observation":null}
