{"bundle_id":"53ff303773fefc00166fcbbbafcad428","candidates":[{"id":"redis2/orphan-cleanup-zrem-error-skips-restore","verdict":"confirmed","basis":"The listing-time ZREM is new at head. Base never removed members in the not-found branch, so the change adds this removal. The change's own repair (commit 6c8fde6) is meant to restore the member when a concurrent insert recreated the value. Its ZREM-error branch returns before that repair. A go-redis error does not prove the server skipped the ZREM: a lost reply or read timeout after the command was written is one case. In that case the interleaving is: Set (value written), ZAddNX (no-op, member still present), ZREM (executed, reply lost). The live value is left without an index member. Nothing re-adds it: UpdateEntry only calls doInsertEntry, and ListDirectoryEntries and DeleteFolderChildren enumerate only the ZSET. I could not run a Redis test. The confirmation rests on tracing the code.","evidence":[{"coordinate":"weed/filer/redis2/universal_redis_store.go:238-240","text":"if err := store.Client.ZRem(ctx, dirListKey, fileName).Err(); err != nil {
		return
	}"},{"coordinate":"weed/filer/redis2/universal_redis_store.go:56-74","text":"InsertEntry: doInsertEntry (Set) first, then ZAddNX of the member; ZAddNX is a no-op if the member is present"},{"coordinate":"weed/filer/redis2/universal_redis_store.go:96-98","text":"UpdateEntry: return store.doInsertEntry(ctx, entry) (never touches the index ZSET)"},{"coordinate":"git diff db5a086 6c8fde6 -- weed/filer/redis2/universal_redis_store.go","text":"@@ -205,6 +205,7 @@ + store.removeOrphanedDirectoryListMember(ctx, dirListKey, path, fileName) (base had no removal in the ErrNotFound branch)"},{"coordinate":"commit-6c8fde6/"Restore the member when the value is present again after the removal"","text":"The change promises to keep the member when a concurrent insert recreates the value, so the error-return branch leaves that promise unmet."},{"coordinate":"go-redis v9.21.0 error.go:102-105","text":"if errors.Is(err, context.Canceled) || errors.Is(err, context.DeadlineExceeded) { return false }"}],"corrections":{"action":"must-fix","change":"State the rule as: a live value key must never be observed without its member in the directory ZSET, because InsertEntry writes the value before the member. Restore that for every ZREM outcome, not only ZREM success. (1) Do not return on a ZREM error. Fall through to the EXISTS re-check and the ZAddNX restore, which is a no-op when the member is present. (2) A context cancellation or deadline error leaves the same ctx unusable for the follow-up EXISTS and ZAddNX, so the compensation must run on a context not tied to the request, for example context.WithoutCancel(ctx) with its own short timeout. Otherwise the fix covers only reply-loss and read-timeout errors. (3) The EXISTS re-check must be answered by the master. In a cluster with readOnly, routeByLatency or routeRandomly, EXISTS is a read-only command and can go to a replica, so lag can report 0 for a value just written on the master. Re-check through a master-routed command or not through a replica-routed read. See the steady-state ruling below."},"safety_rulings":[{"path":"removeOrphanedDirectoryListMember when ZREM succeeds, then EXISTS and ZAddNX, on a single or sentinel client or a cluster with default settings (steady state, no error)","conditions":"An InsertEntry lands at any point between FindEntry's not-found and the end of the cleanup. The insert's Set happens before or after the ZREM, and its ZAddNX happens before or after the ZREM.","premise":"The rule holds without errors on this path: a live value is never left without a member.","ruling":"holds","evidence":[{"coordinate":"weed/filer/redis2/universal_redis_store.go:246-250","text":"exists, err := store.Client.Exists(ctx, store.getKey(string(path))).Result()
	if err == nil && exists == 0 {
		return
	}

	store.Client.ZAddNX(ctx, dirListKey, redis.Z{Score: 0, Member: fileName})"},{"coordinate":"weed/filer/redis2/universal_redis_store.go:56-74","text":"If the insert's ZAddNX runs after the ZREM, the member is absent and it is added. If it ran before the ZREM (a no-op), the Set already happened, so EXISTS returns 1 and the member is restored. A Set after an EXISTS of 0 is followed by a ZAddNX that finds the member absent and adds it."},{"coordinate":"weed/filer/redis2/universal_redis_store.go:39-42 (getKey)","text":"The value key and the member both go through the master when readOnly is false, so ordering is by a single server for this key pair in the non-cluster case."}]},{"path":"removeOrphanedDirectoryListMember EXISTS re-check on a cluster client with readOnly, routeByLatency or routeRandomly (steady state, no errors)","conditions":"The cluster store is configured with readOnly=true or routeByLatency=true. A concurrent InsertEntry Set lands on the master. The replica has not yet applied it when EXISTS runs.","premise":"The EXISTS re-check reflects the master's current state.","ruling":"fails","evidence":[{"coordinate":"go-redis v9.21.0 osscluster.go:205-207","text":"if opt.RouteByLatency || opt.RouteRandomly {
		opt.ReadOnly = true
	}"},{"coordinate":"go-redis v9.21.0 osscluster.go:2399-2404","text":"if c.opt.ReadOnly {
		cmdInfo := c.cmdInfo(ctx, cmdName)
		if cmdInfo != nil && cmdInfo.ReadOnly {
			return c.slotReadOnlyNode(state, slot)
		}
	}
	return state.slotMasterNode(slot)"},{"coordinate":"weed/command/scaffold/filer.toml:287-290","text":"# allows reads from slave servers or the master, but all writes still go to the master
readOnly = false
# automatically use the closest Redis server for reads
routeByLatency = false"},{"coordinate":"weed/filer/redis2/universal_redis_store.go:246-250","text":"A stale exists == 0 makes the function return without ZAddNX. That leaves the value without a member, the same end state as the candidate, with no error involved. This path is opt-in (defaults are false) and needs replication lag inside the race window."}]},{"path":"ZREM error path when the value is genuinely absent (candidate's proposed fall-through)","conditions":"ZREM errors, or executed but the reply was lost. No concurrent insert has happened.","premise":"The proposed fall-through is safe: it cannot resurrect a genuine orphan.","ruling":"holds","evidence":[{"coordinate":"weed/filer/redis2/universal_redis_store.go:246-248","text":"if err == nil && exists == 0 { return }"},{"coordinate":"weed/filer/redis2/universal_redis_store.go:250","text":"store.Client.ZAddNX(...) restores only when EXISTS reports the value present or the check failed. If EXISTS is 0, the fall-through returns without restoring. If EXISTS itself errors, the restore leaves a possible orphan in the ZSET, and a later listing retries the cleanup."}]}]}],"premises":[],"duplicate_groups":[],"observation":null}
